Title: Keep ATL thunk emulation on in the browser process before Vista
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo)

On a Windows XP machine with hardware NX and Office 2003 installed, Electron
died shortly after start with "Data Execution Prevention closed this
program". The report was

  EventType : BEX  P1 : electron.exe  P7 : 00105d08  P8 : c0000005  P9 : 00000008

an execute fault at a heap address, called from user32's window procedure
dispatch. The bytes there were

  c7 44 24 04 00 5d 10 00   mov dword ptr [esp+4], 00105d00h
  e9 fb f7 5a 13            jmp SKCHUI.DLL+5510h

which is an ATL window thunk. SKCHUI.DLL is Office's handwriting input, a
text service the language bar loads into every process that has a window.

The browser process asks for DEP with MITIGATION_DEP_NO_ATL_THUNK, which
turns off the kernel's emulation of exactly this sequence. That is the right
choice where no such DLL exists any more. Before Vista they are common, so
leave emulation on there: the kernel emulates only the known ATL thunk
patterns, and everything else on the heap is still not executable.

It never showed in a virtual machine because the guests ran without NX, where
this mitigation does nothing.

diff --git a/content/app/sandbox_helper_win.cc b/content/app/sandbox_helper_win.cc
index 07ef39eb4c..100be807b8 100644
--- a/content/app/sandbox_helper_win.cc
+++ b/content/app/sandbox_helper_win.cc
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 
 #include "content/public/app/sandbox_helper_win.h"
 
+#include "base/win/windows_version.h"
 #include "sandbox/win/src/sandbox.h"
 #include "sandbox/win/src/sandbox_factory.h"
 
@@ -16,9 +17,19 @@ void InitializeSandboxInfo(sandbox::SandboxInterfaceInfo* info,
     info->broker_services->SetStartingMitigations(starting_mitigations);
 
     // Ensure the proper mitigations are enforced for the browser process.
-    info->broker_services->RatchetDownSecurityMitigations(
-        sandbox::MITIGATION_DEP | sandbox::MITIGATION_DEP_NO_ATL_THUNK |
-        sandbox::MITIGATION_HARDEN_TOKEN_IL_POLICY);
+    sandbox::MitigationFlags browser_mitigations =
+        sandbox::MITIGATION_DEP | sandbox::MITIGATION_HARDEN_TOKEN_IL_POLICY;
+    // Before Vista, leave ATL thunk emulation on. Text services and input
+    // method DLLs of that era are loaded into every process that has a
+    // window, and some build their window procedures as ATL thunks on the
+    // heap -- Office 2003's handwriting input (SKCHUI.DLL) is one. With
+    // emulation off, the first message to such a window is a DEP violation
+    // that takes the browser down. The kernel only emulates the exact ATL
+    // thunk byte sequences, so everything else on the heap stays protected.
+    if (base::win::GetVersion() >= base::win::Version::VISTA) {
+      browser_mitigations |= sandbox::MITIGATION_DEP_NO_ATL_THUNK;
+    }
+    info->broker_services->RatchetDownSecurityMitigations(browser_mitigations);
     // Note: these mitigations are "post-startup".  Some mitigations that need
     // to be enabled sooner (e.g. MITIGATION_EXTENSION_POINT_DISABLE) are done
     // so in Chrome_ELF.
